# MY LINUX LEARNING DAY-02
**whoami**: displays the username of the current user logged into the terminal.
**df -h[disk free]**: it is used to check the storage of server. important for checking EBS volume in AWS.
**free -h[free memory]**: displays how much memory is utilized or free.
**top**: this command list all the running programs live ranked by how much CPU and RAM they are stealing. enter 'q' so that you can exit out of it.
**ps aux**: instead of live updating it takes static snapshot of all running program.
